\fs64 \cf2 Pointer types\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 The Mojo standard library includes several pointer types with different characteristics:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/memory/pointer/Pointer/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul Pointer}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
 is a safe pointer that points to a single value that it doesn't own.\
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/memory/owned_pointer/OwnedPointer/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul OwnedPointer}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
 is a smart pointer that points to a single value, and maintains exclusive ownership of that value.\
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/memory/arc_pointer/ArcPointer/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul ArcPointer}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
 is a reference-counted smart pointer that points to an owned value with ownership potentially shared with other instances of 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ArcPointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/memory/unsafe_pointer/UnsafePointer/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul UnsafePointer}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
 points to one or more consecutive memory locations, and can refer to uninitialized memory.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
