\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Unlike an 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 OwnedPointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , an 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ArcPointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  can be freely copied. All instances of a given 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ArcPointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  share a reference count, which is incremented whenever the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ArcPointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  is copied and decremented whenever an instance is destroyed. When the reference count reaches zero, the stored value is destroyed and the allocated memory is freed.\
You can use 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ArcPointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  to implement safe reference-semantic types. For example, in the following code snippet 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 SharedDict
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  uses an 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ArcPointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  to store a dictionary. Copying an instance of 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 SharedDict
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  only copies the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 ArcPointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , not the dictionary, which is shared between all of the copies.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb13 from\cf14  std\cf5 .\cf14 memory \cf5 import\cf14  ArcPointer\cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb13 struct\cf14  \cf19 SharedDict\cf5 (\cf14 Copyable\cf5 ):\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13     \cf5 var\cf14  attributes\cf5 :\cf14  ArcPointer\cf5 [\cf14 Dict\cf5 [\cf14 String\cf5 ,\cf14  String\cf5 ]]\cf14 \cb1 \
\
\cb13     \cf5 def\cf14  \cf19 __init__\cf5 (out\cf14  self\cf5 ):\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13         attributesDict\cf5 :\cf14  Dict\cf5 [\cf14 String\cf5 ,\cf14  String\cf5 ]\cf14  \cf5 =\cf14  \cf5 \{\}\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13         self\cf5 .\cf14 attributes \cf5 =\cf14  ArcPointer\cf5 (\cf14 attributesDict\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\
\cb13     \cf5 def\cf14  \cf19 __init__\cf5 (out\cf14  self\cf5 ,\cf14  \cf5 *,\cf14  copy\cf5 :\cf14  Self\cf5 ):\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13         self\cf5 .\cf14 attributes \cf5 =\cf14  copy\cf5 .\cf14 attributes\cb1 \
\
\cb13     \cf5 def\cf14  \cf19 __setitem__\cf5 (mut\cf14  self\cf5 ,\cf14  key\cf5 :\cf14  String\cf5 ,\cf14  value\cf5 :\cf14  String\cf5 )\cf14  raises\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13         self\cf5 .\cf14 attributes\cf5 [][\cf14 key\cf5 ]\cf14  \cf5 =\cf14  value\cb1 \
\
\cb13     \cf5 def\cf14  \cf19 __getitem__\cf5 (\cf14 self\cf5 ,\cf14  key\cf5 :\cf14  String\cf5 )\cf14  raises \cf5 ->\cf14  String\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13         \cf5 return\cf14  self\cf5 .\cf14 attributes\cf5 [].\cf14 get\cf5 (\cf14 key\cf5 ,\cf14  default\cf5 =\cf20 ""\cf5 )\cf14 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb13 def\cf14  \cf19 main\cf5 ()\cf14  raises\cf5 :\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13     thing1 \cf5 =\cf14  SharedDict\cf5 ()\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13     thing2 \cf5 =\cf14  thing1\cb1 \
\cb13     thing1\cf5 [\cf20 "Flip"\cf5 ]\cf14  \cf5 =\cf14  \cf20 "Flop"\cf14 \cb1 \
\cb13     \cf5 print(\cf14 thing2\cf5 [\cf20 "Flip"\cf5 ])\cf14 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

